{"data": [{"author_id": "2114906570303905792", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:18:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118498193239413078"], "id": "2118498193239413078", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1382303733040693249", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118443193104842951", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SergioMarakis @kimmonismus Exactly; a short clip can make cheap creative tests feasible, but a clear hook still earns the view.", "url": "https://x.com/BudgtStore/status/2118498193239413078"}, {"author_id": "2114906570303905792", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:17:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118497960162201705"], "id": "2118497960162201705", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118396513541857743", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus That cost makes polished-enough ad testing accessible to small teams; distribution and concept still do the heavy lifting.", "url": "https://x.com/BudgtStore/status/2118497960162201705"}, {"author_id": "1749080389426327552", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:37:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118472811014770894"], "id": "2118472811014770894", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118396513541857743", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus The noodle wok test I ran on Omni was solid on faces but the noodles turned to mush around 4 seconds in. If the consistency fix holds up in a similar test this becomes very usable for quick clips.", "url": "https://x.com/ziroel_98/status/2118472811014770894"}, {"author_id": "1382303733040693249", "cr